	(descr "Keystone 1287 PC quick-fit male tab, 0.250 in (6.35 mm) Faston-style, vertical, two solder legs. Source: Keystone Electronics catalog page M65p59 (PC Quick-Fit Male Tabs, .250 (6.4) Tab, cat. no. 1287), mirrored from https://cdn.components.ru/media/PDF/412259.pdf (Keystone's own site refused the fetch): legs 0.050 (1.27) wide at the shoulder and 0.045 (1.14) at the tip, 0.032 (0.80) brass, leg pitch 0.200 (5.1), mounting holes 0.052 (1.3) dia., tab 0.312 (7.9) above the board. Origin on the tab's mating axis, midway between the legs; the tab plane runs along x. Pads 1 and 2 are the TWO LEGS OF ONE TERMINAL: give both the same net. UNSOURCED: pad diameter 2.4, courtyard (pad edge + 0.25), silk. CAUTION: the leg section's diagonal (1.27 x 0.80 -> 1.50) is larger than Keystone's 1.3 hole; Keystone states 1.3 and that is what is drawn, but check one physical part in a 1.3 hole before ordering a board.")
